<article class="enc-article">
<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dilawar Khan Ghuri</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1406</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dilawar Khan Ghuri was the founder of the Malwa Sultanate in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. Appointed governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malwa">Malwa</a> by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tughlaq-dynasty">Tughlaq</a> sultans in 1392, he ruled independently after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a> sacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a> in 1398 and took royal state around 1401, ruling from Dhar. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hoshang-shah">Hoshang Shah</a> moved the capital to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mandu">Mandu</a>.</p></div>
